1. DEFINITIONS

   "the Engine" means the Tiamot voxel engine, including the contents of the
   crates/ directory and any other portion of this distribution carrying the
   SPDX identifier GPL-3.0-only.

   "the Scripting API" means the Lua-callable interface the Engine exposes to
   mods, together with the Lua stubs, type definitions, and documentation
   distributed under the api/ directory.

   "the Network Protocol" means the wire protocol spoken between an Engine
   server and an Engine client.

   "an Independent Work" means a work that interacts with the Engine solely
   through the Scripting API, the Network Protocol, or both.


2. GRANT

   Iridesium hereby grants permission to develop, use, reproduce, distribute,
   sell, and license Independent Works under terms of the author's own
   choosing, including terms that are proprietary or otherwise incompatible
   with the GPL.

   For the avoidance of doubt, an Independent Work is not a derivative work of
   the Engine, is not a "modified version" or "work based on the Program" as
   those terms are used in the GPL, and carries no obligation under the GPL by
   reason of its interaction with the Engine.  This holds regardless of whether
   the interaction occurs in a shared address space, whether the Independent
   Work is loaded into a process running Engine code, and whether the Engine
   and the Independent Work are distributed together.

   This permission extends to the output of an Independent Work and to any
   data, assets, or world content it produces.


3. WHAT THIS GRANT DOES NOT COVER

   This permission applies only to interaction through the Scripting API and
   the Network Protocol.  It does not apply to a work that:

   (a) incorporates, links against, or embeds any part of the Engine's source
       or object code otherwise than through the Scripting API or the Network
       Protocol;

   (b) is a modified version of the Engine, or contains a modified copy of any
       part of the Engine; or

   (c) extends the Engine through any private, internal, or unpublished
       interface, or through a Rust plugin, native shared library, or other
       mechanism that is not the Scripting API or the Network Protocol.

   A work of that kind remains subject to the GPL in full.  Modifications to
   the Engine itself must be released under the GPL, whether or not they are
   made in order to support an Independent Work.


4. NO EFFECT ON THE ENGINE'S OWN TERMS

   Nothing in this document alters the terms under which the Engine itself is
